sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R2-R4, swamp-vault-design (Vaultwarden = human copy). docs/reference/vaultwarden.md#sync.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: vault:sync
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VW icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VW as Vaultwarden<br/>vault.orbit Route
  CLI->>GW: vault:sync<br/>--json
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit vault:sync`
  %%> - syntax: `[--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> When:
  %%> - the Gateway admits the same sync itself when a database credential changes, and once an hour to repair drift
  %%> - run the command to see the result at once
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no per-minute poll; nothing runs while nothing changed, except the hourly check
  Note over GW: Build the wanted items<br/>task #5168 · items to vault
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the `vault` extension is on and Vaultwarden is set up, else `vault.not_configured`
  %%> - no other setup, sync or teardown runs; a busy sync waits briefly, then returns `vault.sync_busy`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - builds one Database item per MySQL and PostgreSQL connection and Database user with a stored password; others are listed as skipped
  %%> - pushes the wanted items and the account secrets to the Swamp vault as `vault-sync-5168` after commit (R3)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5168 recorded with the publishing ledger as input
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-vault-sync
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); no Node is a target
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the setup, the ledger of published item IDs and sources, and the vault key names; never a password
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5168
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`, then prints `vault:status`
  SW->>VW: Log in and unlock<br/>bw login · unlock · sync
  %%> How:
  %%> - the official Bitwarden CLI on 209, in a scratch home, trusting only the Orbit root CA
  %%> - secrets come from `vault.get`, in the environment of each command
  SW->>VW: Read the collection<br/>bw list items · trash
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the collection's items and the trash, and finds Orbit's items by their `orbit.source` field
  Note over SW: Plan the changes<br/>create · rewrite · adopt · delete
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates missing items, rewrites changed ones, adopts an item for a wanted source the ledger lacks
  %%> - deletes a recorded item whose source is gone, only when its ID and source match the ledger
  %%> Leaves:
  %%> - items without `orbit.source`, and copies the ledger does not name
  SW->>VW: Delete gone items<br/>bw delete --permanent
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - deletes each planned item permanently, one per step
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - an item that also belongs to another visible collection: `vault.item_shared`
  SW->>VW: Write the items<br/>bw create · bw edit
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates or rewrites each planned item as a Secure Note with the Database item fields, one per step
  SW->>VW: Log out<br/>bw logout · remove scratch home
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - logs out and deletes the scratch home, on success and on failure
  alt every change made
    VW-->>SW: items match
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - each item's ID and source
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · item IDs
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Update the ledger<br/>last_synced_at · task done
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the publishing ledger records each item ID; `vault:status` shows the new `last_synced_at`
    %%> - task #5168 succeeds
  else a change fails
    VW--xSW: refused or no answer
    %%> When:
    %%> - login or unlock fails, Vaultwarden is down, or a create, edit or delete fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its safe error code
    Note over GW: Keep the ledger<br/>last_error · vault.sync_failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the ledger stays unchanged; `vault:status` shows `last_error`; task #5168 fails
    %%> In Vaultwarden:
    %%> - changes made before the failure stay
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - safe: the next sync reads the collection again and adopts items a lost reply created
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5168
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
